fix(integrity): correct the defects of the 21 September review (R-11 to R-14)

The review raised the project to 6.19 and recognised the real work, but recorded
three things that got worse and one I caused. All four are now fixed.

- R-11. The authorisation attributed to the docente was dated 19 September in
  two files (OBSERVACIONES.md and SRS-v1.1.0.tex). It is in writing in his
  evaluation of 20 September, section 2, as VERSIONING.md already said. Both
  citations are corrected and the SRS is recompiled.
- R-12. Four files claimed the SUS instrument predates every session. Its
  history shows the last change is b9cac65, of 20 September at 18:05, and that
  it rewrites seven of the ten items, so the sessions of the 19th used the
  earlier wording. The false claim is replaced by the verifiable chronology and
  declared as a limitation, in ETHICS.md, SRS-v1.3.0.tex,
  sus-analysis-2026-09.md and registro-aceptacion.md.
- R-13. The rename commit claimed "0 of 172 methods in main and 0 of 25 in test
  carry a Spanish name". A proper count, splitting identifiers into words so
  that "create" no longer reads as "crear", finds 96 Spanish names in src/test.
  The backend and frontend renames are completed here: six repository and
  service methods and twenty-five frontend methods, with their template call
  sites. What remains in main and in the frontend is either a detector false
  positive (findById, catchError) or imposed by the schema or the JSON contract
  (findByCodigo, findFirstByActivoTrueOrderByIdVehiculoAsc, getFechaProgramada,
  getComentario), which is exactly what broke the contract a round earlier.
- R-14. My own defect: the global replacement that updated the DOI also changed
  cff-version, which is the schema version, leaving CITATION.cff invalid.

Also in this round:

- The expediente no longer declares P5 at 0 %. It records the September study
  and runs calcular_sus.py, so the detector the review found unwired is wired.
- The integrity verifier grows by sixteen checks, to 52: the validity of
  cff-version, the compiled PDFs and the captures are not stubs, the SUS mean
  recomputed from the raw CSV matches what the SRS and the analysis declare,
  the session dates, the ten instrument items, and no placeholder javadoc.
- CONTRIBUCIONES.md declares this round's work, including the eighty javadocs
  and the renames, which the review found missing from the expediente.

Verified: mvn test-compile BUILD SUCCESS, ng build clean, integrity 52/52,
mutations 9 of 9 with zero survivors.
